  "statement": "Given an integer `n`, return _all the structurally unique **BST'**s (binary search trees), which has exactly_ `n` _nodes of unique values from_ `1` _to_ `n`. Return the answer in **any order**.\n\n**Example 1:**\n\n![](./assets/unique-binary-search-trees-ii-1.jpg)\n```\nInput: n = 3\nOutput: [[1,null,2,null,3],[1,null,3,2],[2,1,3],[3,1,null,null,2],[3,2,null,1]]\n```\n\n**Example 2:**\n\n```\nInput: n = 1\nOutput: [[1]]\n```\n\n**Constraints:**\n\n*   `1 <= n <= 8`",
